1
00:04:15,502 --> 00:04:18,096
- It 's in there . Number nine . - Right .

2
00:04:52,872 --> 00:04:54,863
Don 't stand around . Go on home , all of you .

3
00:04:55,041 --> 00:04:57,669
- What happened , constable ? - Well ...

4
00:04:57,877 --> 00:05:00,072
- ... there 's been another murder . - A murder .

5
00:05:00,246 --> 00:05:03,477
There 's nothing you can do . I told you to go home . Go on .

6
00:05:08,521 --> 00:05:10,386
Oh , just a minute , miss .

7
00:05:10,557 --> 00:05:12,252
Are you alone ?

8
00:05:12,559 --> 00:05:14,754
You work out at the Warren home , don 't you ?

9
00:05:14,928 --> 00:05:16,452
That 's nearly two miles from here .

10
00:05:16,630 --> 00:05:19,428
You 'd better hurry if you 're gonna get there before dark .

11
00:05:27,774 --> 00:05:31,141
- Got any ideas who did it , constable ? - Yeah .

12
00:05:31,378 --> 00:05:34,404
Same fella did the first one . Same fella did the second one .

13
00:05:34,581 --> 00:05:35,878
But who he is , I don 't know .

14
00:05:36,049 --> 00:05:38,210
Somebody in this town . Somebody we all know .

15
00:05:38,385 --> 00:05:42,947
Somebody we see every day . Might be me . Might be you .

16
00:05:43,123 --> 00:05:44,750
Why , how could- - ? I mean ...

17
00:05:44,924 --> 00:05:47,950
- ... I was here at my desk , anyway . - Oh , be quiet .

18
00:06:04,044 --> 00:06:06,012
Didn 't know you was called , Dr. Parry .

19
00:06:06,179 --> 00:06:09,307
I wasn 't . As I was leaving the office , I heard about the murder .

20
00:06:09,482 --> 00:06:11,541
Thought I 'd see if there 's anything I could do .

21
00:06:11,718 --> 00:06:14,278
Well , there ain 't . Unless , of course

22
00:06:14,654 --> 00:06:16,679
you 're good enough to uncork a miracle

23
00:06:16,856 --> 00:06:18,653
and bring the dead back to life .

24
00:06:18,825 --> 00:06:20,725
I don 't think I 'm that good .

25
00:06:20,927 --> 00:06:23,725
There 's no sense in you going up . She 's dead , all right .

26
00:06:23,897 --> 00:06:27,230
Dr. Harvey 's up there , and that 's what he says . She 's dead .

27
00:06:27,367 --> 00:06:30,302
Well , in that event , constable , I certainly can 't do her any harm .

28
00:06:36,910 --> 00:06:39,640
- Hello , Parry . - Dr . Harvey .

29
00:06:39,779 --> 00:06:42,680
There 's nothing for you to do , unless you 're sightseeing .

30
00:06:42,849 --> 00:06:44,646
- How was she killed ? - Strangled .

31
00:06:44,818 --> 00:06:47,184
- She was dead when we got here . - Who was she ?

32
00:06:47,353 --> 00:06:50,652
That lame girl that worked over at Nelson 's .

33
00:06:53,159 --> 00:06:54,854
How awful .

34
00:06:55,995 --> 00:06:57,929
She was just in my office last week .

35
00:06:58,098 --> 00:07:01,966
Did she pay her bill or was this her way of getting out of it ?

36
00:07:02,669 --> 00:07:05,137
I haven 't enough experience to make that sort of joke .

37
00:07:05,305 --> 00:07:06,966
Perhaps not , Dr. Parry .

38
00:07:07,140 --> 00:07:09,165
- I 'll run along . - Oh , just a minute .

39
00:07:09,409 --> 00:07:11,877
I hear you were over to see Mr. Stover last night .

40
00:07:12,045 --> 00:07:14,411
- Yes , I was . - Don 't you know he 's my patient ?

41
00:07:14,581 --> 00:07:16,242
I only went because they called me .

42
00:07:16,416 --> 00:07:18,714
They told me that you 'd refused to go until morning .

43
00:07:18,885 --> 00:07:22,218
- I thought it might be serious . - You 've got a lot to learn , young fella .

44
00:07:22,388 --> 00:07:25,653
You 've only been here a short time . I 've been here for a good many years .

45
00:07:25,859 --> 00:07:29,522
If I answered all the calls as they came , I wouldn 't get any sleep at all .

46
00:07:29,696 --> 00:07:32,722
Well , that 's why I think there 's room for two doctors in this town .

47
00:07:32,899 --> 00:07:35,697
Reckon so , but let the competition be on an open plane . Ethics .

48
00:07:35,869 --> 00:07:37,131
You get what I mean , Parry ?

49
00:07:37,303 --> 00:07:39,863
If ever I 'm called on an emergency , and you 're sleeping

50
00:07:40,039 --> 00:07:41,529
I intend to go .

51
00:07:41,708 --> 00:07:45,769
That 's very noble and ambitious . Don 't let anything discourage you .

52
00:07:45,945 --> 00:07:47,503
Nothing will .

53
00:07:47,714 --> 00:07:49,375
Oh , by the way

54
00:07:49,849 --> 00:07:52,044
you might like to see what the Stovers did

55
00:07:52,218 --> 00:07:54,345
to that prescription you wrote last night .

56
00:08:21,247 --> 00:08:24,910
I 'm gonna make some calls , Helen . I 'll take you to the crossroads .

57
00:08:25,919 --> 00:08:27,853
Were you at the hotel ?

58
00:08:28,621 --> 00:08:31,818
Wasn 't a very nice thing to have happen on your afternoon off .

59
00:08:32,992 --> 00:08:34,550
I 've been pretty busy lately .

60
00:08:34,794 --> 00:08:37,285
I haven 't had much of a chance to drop in and see you .

61
00:08:37,497 --> 00:08:40,057
But I 've been thinking about you a great deal .

62
00:08:40,834 --> 00:08:44,133
You haven 't any family , Helen . No one else to worry about you .

63
00:08:44,537 --> 00:08:47,973
And I got to wondering just how long you were going on like this .

64
00:08:48,141 --> 00:08:51,599
I mean , doing the work you 're doing at the Warrens ' .

65
00:08:52,278 --> 00:08:55,475
You wanted to be a nurse or a teacher .

66
00:08:56,950 --> 00:08:58,747
You mean , you 're going to give up that

67
00:08:58,918 --> 00:09:02,319
without making an effort to get your voice back again ?

68
00:09:03,957 --> 00:09:06,949
Yes , I know , Helen , you did see a doctor once .

69
00:09:07,126 --> 00:09:08,684
That was a long time ago .

70
00:09:08,862 --> 00:09:11,228
They might have discovered a lot since then .

71
00:09:11,397 --> 00:09:14,127
There are specialists in Boston now .

72
00:09:15,935 --> 00:09:18,768
I don 't want to build your hopes up , Helen

73
00:09:18,938 --> 00:09:21,930
but it seems such a shame to give up so easily .

74
00:09:23,710 --> 00:09:26,406
You 'd rather I wouldn 't talk about it , wouldn 't you ?

75
00:09:27,814 --> 00:09:30,476
All right , I won 't .

76
00:09:39,058 --> 00:09:41,253
You know the words to that tune ?

77
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,730
Dr. Parry .

78
00:09:55,909 --> 00:09:57,774
Dr. Parry .

79
00:10:01,848 --> 00:10:04,612
- Hello , Freddy . - Pa 's sick , Dr. Parry , bad .

80
00:10:04,784 --> 00:10:06,081
They didn 't send you for me ?

81
00:10:06,252 --> 00:10:09,415
Ma sent me for Dr. Harvey , but Pa wants you to come .

82
00:10:09,756 --> 00:10:12,384
I 'm afraid I can 't help you out this time , Freddy .

83
00:10:12,558 --> 00:10:15,083
You don 't understand . Your father 's Dr. Harvey 's patient .

84
00:10:15,295 --> 00:10:18,662
We 'll have to try and find him for you . I 'll call him as soon as I get home .

85
00:10:18,831 --> 00:10:22,198
Oh , please , Dr. Parry , you come . I want you to come .

86
00:10:23,436 --> 00:10:25,904
All right , come on , get in . We 'll go up and have a look .

87
00:10:26,072 --> 00:10:28,040
I 'll run you home afterwards .

88
00:10:28,207 --> 00:10:29,936
Afraid you 'll be late ?

89
00:10:33,913 --> 00:10:35,778
Are you sure you 'll be all right ?

90
00:10:35,949 --> 00:10:38,179
You 'll go straight home , won 't you , Helen ?

91
00:13:55,047 --> 00:13:58,574
Oh , it 's you . Thank heavens .

92
00:13:58,985 --> 00:14:01,579
They phoned us about the murder .

93
00:14:02,054 --> 00:14:05,080
For a while I thought it might have been you .

94
00:14:08,327 --> 00:14:11,160
It 's terrible . That 's what it is .

95
00:14:11,364 --> 00:14:12,854
Horrible .

96
00:14:13,032 --> 00:14:15,466
As if it isn 't bad enough murdering people

97
00:14:15,635 --> 00:14:18,263
but all these defenseless women .

98
00:14:18,437 --> 00:14:21,099
First there was the girl with a scar on her face .

99
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:24,434
Then that poor simple-minded creature

100
00:14:24,610 --> 00:14:28,239
and now this cripple . It seems like ... .

101
00:14:28,648 --> 00:14:30,639
I guess you 've had enough for one afternoon .

102
00:14:30,816 --> 00:14:34,013
Now- - Now , get your wet shoes off before you catch your death .

103
00:14:34,187 --> 00:14:36,621
And you 'd better get up to Mrs. Warren straightaway .

104
00:14:36,789 --> 00:14:39,349
She 's raising a rumpus with that nurse of hers again .

105
00:14:39,525 --> 00:14:41,152
Won 't even allow her in the room now .

106
00:14:42,295 --> 00:14:45,958
She sent down word for you to go up the moment you came in .

107
00:14:46,899 --> 00:14:49,163
Is that someone at the front door ?

108
00:15:07,887 --> 00:15:09,752
Who 's there ?

109
00:15:20,199 --> 00:15:21,757
I don 't understand .

110
00:15:21,934 --> 00:15:25,267
I closed that window when the storm started .

111
00:15:26,672 --> 00:15:29,835
I 'll get a hammer and fix that shutter .

112
00:15:45,891 --> 00:15:47,916
It was him !

113
00:15:48,327 --> 00:15:51,023
Carleton , bad dog !

114
00:15:55,735 --> 00:16:00,934
Out all day and only home in time to get under my feet and break my- -

115
00:16:01,374 --> 00:16:03,740
You 're a no-good loafer , that 's what you are .

116
00:16:03,909 --> 00:16:05,570
Criminals and murderers loose

117
00:16:05,745 --> 00:16:08,578
and you 're out courting the neighbor 's dog .

118
00:16:10,783 --> 00:16:15,743
Oh , Carleton , Carleton , you deserve a good beating .

119
00:16:16,255 --> 00:16:18,883
Guess I better dry you first .

120
00:16:19,659 --> 00:16:22,150
You 'll catch your death of cold , that 's what you will .

121
00:16:23,863 --> 00:16:27,959
And if you think this is all I 've got to do , you 're mistaken .

122
00:16:29,402 --> 00:16:31,666
I think I better fix that window first .

123
00:16:31,837 --> 00:16:35,273
And I hope that Carleton is all that came in .

124
00:16:37,376 --> 00:16:41,039
I won 't need you . You 'd better get up to Mrs. Warren .

125
00:18:17,576 --> 00:18:19,066
Helen ?

126
00:18:22,181 --> 00:18:24,911
Haven 't you gone in to Mrs. Warren yet ?

127
00:18:25,251 --> 00:18:27,185
Hurry along , will you ?

128
00:18:42,067 --> 00:18:45,264
It 's about time . Mrs. Warren 's been asking for you all afternoon .

129
00:18:45,438 --> 00:18:47,804
She won 't let me do anything for her . Oh , no .

130
00:18:47,973 --> 00:18:51,636
I 'm ordered to sit out in the hallway . Why in the world am I kept on here

131
00:18:51,811 --> 00:18:54,279
to nurse someone who can 't stand the sight of me ?

132
00:18:54,447 --> 00:18:57,678
But then , I can 't stand the sight of her either .

133
00:18:57,850 --> 00:18:59,681
I 've nursed some queer ones in my time

134
00:18:59,852 --> 00:19:02,685
but she 's got them all beat . She 's sly too .

135
00:19:02,855 --> 00:19:06,518
Even with her eyes shut , she seems to be watching you like an evil spirit .

136
00:19:06,725 --> 00:19:10,320
But get in there before she gets herself into another tantrum .

137
00:20:18,664 --> 00:20:21,326
I got him before he got me .

138
00:20:22,134 --> 00:20:24,102
The tiger , I mean .

139
00:20:24,570 --> 00:20:27,004
I was as good as any man .

140
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:31,173
You 're not only late , but you 're playing games .

141
00:20:31,343 --> 00:20:33,174
Why are you so late ?

142
00:20:35,548 --> 00:20:37,743
Never mind . Never mind .

143
00:20:37,917 --> 00:20:39,612
Come here .

144
00:20:40,986 --> 00:20:43,580
I hoped you were never coming back

145
00:20:44,390 --> 00:20:46,290
that you 'd run away .

146
00:20:48,494 --> 00:20:52,521
Leave this house tonight if you know what 's good for you .

147
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:56,165
You understand ?

148
00:20:56,936 --> 00:20:58,665
Who 's there ?

149
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:07,774
I told you to sit in the hall . Why must you spy on me ?

150
00:21:07,947 --> 00:21:10,245
I 'm not spying on you . It 's time for your medicine .

151
00:21:10,416 --> 00:21:13,874
- Helen can give me my medicine . - I don 't know what I 'm being paid for .

152
00:21:14,053 --> 00:21:18,547
You 're being paid to sit in the hall . That 's all you 're good for . Get out .

153
00:21:42,014 --> 00:21:44,312
That was the constable at the front door , professor .

154
00:21:44,483 --> 00:21:46,075
He wants to see you .

155
00:21:46,251 --> 00:21:48,151
I 've asked him to wait in the living room .

156
00:21:48,320 --> 00:21:49,878
Thank you .

157
00:21:51,690 --> 00:21:54,488
- Put these in order , will you ? - Yes , sir .

158
00:21:56,161 --> 00:21:58,322
- Oh , constable ? - Yes , Professor Warren ?

159
00:21:58,497 --> 00:22:00,055
I 'll be with you in just a moment .

160
00:22:00,299 --> 00:22:03,359
Blanche , get these ready as quickly as possible .

161
00:22:03,535 --> 00:22:05,002
Yes , sir .

162
00:22:09,341 --> 00:22:11,741
- Hello , constable . - Hello , professor .

163
00:22:11,910 --> 00:22:14,242
- Wouldn 't you like to sit down ? - Oh , no . No , thanks .

164
00:22:14,413 --> 00:22:16,938
You sure got a lot of interesting things here .

165
00:22:17,116 --> 00:22:20,313
- What 's this ? - That ? Plant life .

166
00:22:20,686 --> 00:22:23,086
You mean to say you can write a whole book about ...

167
00:22:23,255 --> 00:22:25,917
- ... little stuff like this ? - Yes .

168
00:22:26,325 --> 00:22:28,020
What did you want to see me about ?

169
00:22:28,193 --> 00:22:30,627
Oh , a couple of things , professor .

170
00:22:30,796 --> 00:22:33,424
I hate to bother you at this time of night

171
00:22:33,599 --> 00:22:36,124
but I figure it 's important enough .

172
00:22:38,203 --> 00:22:40,535
You know , there 's been another murder .

173
00:22:40,706 --> 00:22:42,674
Yes , so I 've heard .

174
00:22:42,841 --> 00:22:44,502
What I want to say is

175
00:22:44,677 --> 00:22:47,373
that we 've traced the murderer to this vicinity .

176
00:22:47,546 --> 00:22:51,448
- Are you certain ? - Yes , that 's why I 've come here .

177
00:22:51,684 --> 00:22:54,209
That 's why I 'm asking everyone to be careful .

178
00:22:54,386 --> 00:22:56,320
Keep your doors and windows locked tonight .

179
00:22:56,488 --> 00:22:59,252
Well , I 'll see that your orders are carried out , constable .

180
00:22:59,425 --> 00:23:03,794
I 'm especially worried about that girl who works for you .

181
00:23:03,996 --> 00:23:05,964
- Helen ? - Yes .

182
00:23:06,131 --> 00:23:08,292
You see , every one of those girls murdered

183
00:23:08,467 --> 00:23:11,061
had something the matter with her . Something wrong .

184
00:23:11,236 --> 00:23:12,863
You mean some sort of an affliction ?

185
00:23:13,072 --> 00:23:16,701
Yes . Now , my hunch is that this murderer , whoever he is , is- -

186
00:23:16,875 --> 00:23:19,343
I understand exactly what you mean , and I assure you

187
00:23:19,511 --> 00:23:21,775
that I shall be especially careful about Helen .

188
00:23:21,947 --> 00:23:25,007
As a matter of fact , I 'll see that somebody is with her at all times .

189
00:23:25,184 --> 00:23:26,583
Good .

190
00:23:30,923 --> 00:23:33,915
Oh , you scared the life out of me , Stephen .

191
00:23:34,159 --> 00:23:36,753
I didn 't hear you come in .

192
00:23:40,933 --> 00:23:42,161
Don 't stop typing .

193
00:23:42,367 --> 00:23:45,564
How many times have I asked you not to see me when I 'm working ?

194
00:23:45,738 --> 00:23:47,933
It 's so embarrassing .

195
00:23:48,707 --> 00:23:52,666
- Please , leave me alone . - I can 't stay away from you .

196
00:23:52,878 --> 00:23:55,540
Now , when am I going to see you , and where ?

197
00:23:55,714 --> 00:23:58,740
You 're not going to see me at all if you don 't let me finish this .

198
00:23:58,917 --> 00:24:03,149
But I 'm so bored . I don 't know what to do with myself .

199
00:24:04,356 --> 00:24:08,224
Stephen , you 're going to get us into trouble . Now , please go .

200
00:24:09,228 --> 00:24:10,525
No .

201
00:24:10,963 --> 00:24:13,989
Then I 'll just have to finish this some place else .

202
00:24:15,667 --> 00:24:17,100
Oh , Miss Blanche .

203
00:24:17,269 --> 00:24:19,430
Yes , Mr. Warren .

204
00:24:22,941 --> 00:24:24,465
Stephen .

205
00:24:34,686 --> 00:24:36,017
You remember my stepbrother ?

206
00:24:36,188 --> 00:24:39,089
I sure do . Haven 't seen you in a long time , Mr. Warren .

207
00:24:39,258 --> 00:24:42,159
Heard you were back . How 'd you leave things over in Europe ?

208
00:24:42,327 --> 00:24:44,818
I left everything in order . They like you to .

209
00:24:44,997 --> 00:24:48,398
- Paris must be quite a town . - Yes , it is .

210
00:24:49,001 --> 00:24:50,434
Lots of beautiful women .

211
00:24:50,602 --> 00:24:52,900
From what I 've seen , they 're not so bad here either .

212
00:24:53,071 --> 00:24:55,699
Always wanted to go there myself

213
00:24:55,874 --> 00:24:57,603
but I 've been married since I was 1 6 .

214
00:24:57,776 --> 00:25:00,609
Never had a chance . Must be pretty exciting .

215
00:25:00,779 --> 00:25:03,509
I understand it 's been pretty exciting here for you too .

216
00:25:03,682 --> 00:25:07,118
- Oh , yes , it has been at that . - Wish there was something I could do .

217
00:25:07,286 --> 00:25:09,220
- Don 't think there is . - Stephen

218
00:25:09,388 --> 00:25:12,653
the constable wants to know if anyone left the house today .

219
00:25:12,858 --> 00:25:14,450
Nothing personal , I assure you .

220
00:25:14,626 --> 00:25:16,526
I 've been asked to check up on everybody .

221
00:25:16,695 --> 00:25:18,424
I haven 't been out all day , constable .

222
00:25:18,831 --> 00:25:21,163
That 's all I wanted to know . Thank you very much .

223
00:25:21,333 --> 00:25:23,267
Good night . Don 't forget to lock your doors .

224
00:25:23,435 --> 00:25:24,868
I won 't .

225
00:25:27,639 --> 00:25:30,369
His stepbrother gave him an accusing look .

226
00:25:31,743 --> 00:25:35,144
Oh , professor , could I see you for a moment , please ?

227
00:25:43,222 --> 00:25:45,656
Would you mind calling him ? He doesn 't know me .

228
00:25:45,824 --> 00:25:48,019
You 're not afraid of him , are you ?

229
00:25:48,193 --> 00:25:51,128
- I 'm sure he loves policemen . - I 'm not in uniform .

230
00:25:52,664 --> 00:25:55,462
All right , Carleton , go away .

231
00:25:56,902 --> 00:25:59,735
- Well , good night . - Good night .

232
00:26:10,082 --> 00:26:13,415
Anything wrong , Albert ? Professor ?

233
00:26:13,585 --> 00:26:17,077
I just stopped by to tell them the same thing I told you in town today , Oates .

234
00:26:17,256 --> 00:26:20,191
- See anything on your way home ? - Nope .

235
00:26:22,594 --> 00:26:25,688
- Well , good night , professor . - Good night .

236
00:26:30,369 --> 00:26:33,395
- Your hat , Oates . - Oh , yeah , keep forgetting .

237
00:26:33,572 --> 00:26:35,472
Come along , Carleton .

238
00:26:39,878 --> 00:26:41,106
Evening , Helen .

239
00:26:44,149 --> 00:26:47,812
Helen , I want to talk to you a moment .

240
00:26:49,154 --> 00:26:51,486
Now , Helen , I don 't want to frighten you

241
00:26:51,657 --> 00:26:53,591
but because of what happened in town

242
00:26:53,792 --> 00:26:56,386
we have to be especially careful for the next few days .

243
00:26:57,162 --> 00:27:00,620
If you should see anything outside of this house , or even in it

244
00:27:00,799 --> 00:27:03,529
that makes you suspicious , I want you to let me know .

245
00:27:03,702 --> 00:27:05,966
See that someone else does your outside work .

246
00:27:06,138 --> 00:27:07,765
You stay in the house .

247
00:27:08,173 --> 00:27:10,937
And don 't hesitate to come to me at any hour if you need help .

248
00:27:11,810 --> 00:27:14,745
Now you may go up to my stepmother , if you wish .

249
00:27:22,287 --> 00:27:23,652
Helen

250
00:27:23,822 --> 00:27:25,790
remember what I told you .

251
00:27:25,958 --> 00:27:27,220
Don 't trust anyone .

252
00:27:50,315 --> 00:27:52,715
Leave the fire alone , Helen .

253
00:27:55,153 --> 00:27:59,112
Pack your things , leave this house tonight .

254
00:28:02,527 --> 00:28:04,586
Too many trees

255
00:28:04,763 --> 00:28:07,391
stretch out their branches

256
00:28:07,799 --> 00:28:09,926
knock the window

257
00:28:10,102 --> 00:28:12,036
try to get in .

258
00:28:12,537 --> 00:28:16,906
When it 's dark , they move . I 've seen them .

259
00:28:18,143 --> 00:28:20,543
Creeping up to the house .

260
00:28:21,046 --> 00:28:23,241
Go away , my dear .

261
00:28:26,051 --> 00:28:28,383
You 're such a little girl .

262
00:28:28,687 --> 00:28:31,019
I want to take care of you .

263
00:28:31,323 --> 00:28:35,282
If you won 't leave the house as l- - I ask you to

264
00:28:35,460 --> 00:28:38,827
you must sleep in this room tonight .

265
00:28:39,097 --> 00:28:41,327
Don 't be afraid of me .

266
00:28:41,500 --> 00:28:43,866
I wanna take care of you .

267
00:28:45,003 --> 00:28:46,698
You see

268
00:28:47,372 --> 00:28:50,136
you 're not safe , my dear .

269
00:28:56,548 --> 00:28:58,448
Oh , leave me alone .

270
00:28:58,683 --> 00:29:01,413
You 're worse than Nurse Barker .

271
00:29:01,853 --> 00:29:03,878
Stop fussing .

272
00:29:04,256 --> 00:29:06,053
If you won 't leave the house as I ask

273
00:29:06,224 --> 00:29:08,488
the least you can do is to leave me alone .

274
00:29:08,693 --> 00:29:10,957
Go over there and sit down .

275
00:29:11,897 --> 00:29:13,865
Sit down .

276
00:29:53,138 --> 00:29:56,107
Stay where you are . I don 't need your help .

277
00:30:04,916 --> 00:30:07,544
Mind your own business .

278
00:30:31,343 --> 00:30:34,176
Helen , what is it ?

279
00:30:38,116 --> 00:30:41,210
Mother must be worse . Get Albert .

280
00:30:50,395 --> 00:30:52,329
Give me the brandy , Helen .

281
00:30:54,699 --> 00:30:56,564
It 's empty . Is there any more ?

282
00:30:56,735 --> 00:30:58,532
Give me the ether , then .

283
00:31:00,038 --> 00:31:02,233
Don 't stand there , give me the ether .

284
00:31:23,795 --> 00:31:26,696
Why did you have to come back , Stephen ?

285
00:31:27,032 --> 00:31:30,195
- Why didn 't you stay in Europe ? - Mother .

286
00:31:30,502 --> 00:31:33,596
There 's always trouble when you come , Stephen .

287
00:31:34,606 --> 00:31:36,597
Always trouble .

288
00:31:37,676 --> 00:31:40,201
Why didn 't you stay away ?

289
00:31:41,246 --> 00:31:43,077
I want Dr. Parry .

290
00:31:43,281 --> 00:31:45,647
- Dr . Parry ? - Yes .

291
00:31:45,884 --> 00:31:48,114
You said you didn 't want him here anymore .

292
00:31:48,353 --> 00:31:51,186
You and Albert decided that .

293
00:31:51,723 --> 00:31:53,987
I want Dr. Parry .

294
00:31:54,326 --> 00:31:57,693
Mother , we 've given him a chance . You haven 't improved any .

295
00:31:57,862 --> 00:32:01,662
I 'll never improve with that ancient Dr. Harvey .

296
00:32:02,867 --> 00:32:06,428
Stupid girl . It 's all your fault .

297
00:32:07,372 --> 00:32:09,567
You brought on this attack .

298
00:32:10,108 --> 00:32:14,169
She deliberately refused to let me have my spectacle case .

299
00:32:14,512 --> 00:32:18,471
Mother , Helen wouldn 't have any reason for refusing to give it to you .

300
00:32:18,650 --> 00:32:23,519
Never mind , never mind . We won 't talk about it anymore .

301
00:32:23,688 --> 00:32:26,122
Get out now , both of you .

302
00:32:26,758 --> 00:32:29,318
Go and call Dr. Parry .

303
00:32:33,798 --> 00:32:35,595
Will you be all right ?

304
00:32:35,767 --> 00:32:38,827
After all these years , you ask me if I 'll be all right .

305
00:32:39,004 --> 00:32:40,904
Oh , Stephen .

306
00:32:41,539 --> 00:32:44,167
Get out . Take that ether with you .

307
00:32:46,845 --> 00:32:49,473
Well , Mother , I can see that you 're feeling better already .

308
00:32:49,714 --> 00:32:53,206
I don 't like that ether . I don 't think it does any good .

309
00:32:53,385 --> 00:32:55,649
But Dr. Parry and Dr. Harvey explained to you

310
00:32:55,820 --> 00:32:59,620
that , taken in small quantities , it 's a stimulant rather than a depressant .

311
00:32:59,791 --> 00:33:01,349
It did help you , didn 't it ?

312
00:33:01,526 --> 00:33:03,585
There 's been another murder , hasn 't there ?

313
00:33:05,697 --> 00:33:07,961
Nobody told me .

314
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:11,430
Nobody had to .

315
00:33:12,971 --> 00:33:15,667
I always know everything .

316
00:33:26,217 --> 00:33:28,014
Oh , Blanche .

317
00:33:38,797 --> 00:33:41,493
Oh , Blanche , if you don 't come here I 'll come over

318
00:33:41,666 --> 00:33:45,329
Yes , I 'll come over Yes , I 'll come over

319
00:33:57,215 --> 00:34:01,447
Pale hands I loved beside the Shalimar

320
00:34:03,355 --> 00:34:05,823
Now , now .

321
00:34:07,826 --> 00:34:10,989
Oh , Steve , I 'm so unhappy .

322
00:34:12,163 --> 00:34:13,630
Stephen .

323
00:34:16,568 --> 00:34:19,696
- Where were you this afternoon ? - Why ?

324
00:34:21,106 --> 00:34:23,574
- Those are mine . - I know .

325
00:34:25,910 --> 00:34:27,537
So you 've unmasked me .

326
00:34:27,712 --> 00:34:30,340
Well , I don 't know whether I 've unmasked you or not

327
00:34:30,515 --> 00:34:33,916
but I don 't know why you told him you weren 't out when you were .

328
00:34:34,452 --> 00:34:37,717
Well , to be honest , I didn 't want to discuss it in front of anyone .

329
00:34:37,889 --> 00:34:39,618
Well , how stupid of you .

330
00:34:39,858 --> 00:34:43,385
If anyone had seen you , you would have made it awkward for all of us .

331
00:34:43,628 --> 00:34:45,255
Where were you ?

332
00:34:45,930 --> 00:34:47,192
- Professor , l- - - Blanche

333
00:34:47,365 --> 00:34:49,560
would you be good enough to leave us ?

334
00:35:00,345 --> 00:35:01,607
Let 's stop sparring .

335
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:04,408
You 're angry because I took Blanche out .

336
00:35:05,216 --> 00:35:07,150
You 're angry because since I 've been home

337
00:35:07,318 --> 00:35:10,583
Blanche and I have gotten to know each other pretty well .

338
00:35:10,755 --> 00:35:12,882
You know , Stephen , you always did smirk

339
00:35:13,091 --> 00:35:14,649
even when you were a child .

340
00:35:14,826 --> 00:35:18,091
It 's one of the things my father disliked about you .

341
00:35:18,396 --> 00:35:20,591
He was my father too .

342
00:35:21,466 --> 00:35:24,629
I 'm inclined to think that Father was disappointed in both of us .

343
00:35:24,803 --> 00:35:27,601
Neither of us fitted his concept of what a real man should be :

344
00:35:27,772 --> 00:35:31,299
A gun-toting , hard-drinking , tough-living , God-fearing citizen .

345
00:35:32,710 --> 00:35:34,405
He always used to say :

346
00:35:34,579 --> 00:35:37,104
" The strong survive , the weak die . "

347
00:35:38,183 --> 00:35:40,549
How wrong he was , Albert

348
00:35:40,718 --> 00:35:43,312
because you and I

349
00:35:43,721 --> 00:35:45,279
the meek

350
00:35:46,491 --> 00:35:48,857
have inherited the earth .

351
00:35:50,829 --> 00:35:52,956
I 'll be honest with you , Stephen .

352
00:35:53,164 --> 00:35:56,099
I don 't like you . I never have .

353
00:35:56,301 --> 00:35:57,962
I have never trusted you .

354
00:35:58,136 --> 00:36:00,627
And you 're quite right when you say that I don 't like

355
00:36:00,805 --> 00:36:03,273
this interest you have in Blanche .

356
00:36:03,475 --> 00:36:04,942
And I 'll tell you something else .

357
00:36:05,109 --> 00:36:07,737
I 've had the responsibility of your mother , not mine

358
00:36:07,912 --> 00:36:10,847
for years , and I 'm tired and strained .

359
00:36:11,015 --> 00:36:13,108
Therefore , I think we should make a decision .

360
00:36:13,318 --> 00:36:15,980
Either you make up your mind to go away permanently

361
00:36:16,154 --> 00:36:19,521
or , if you like , you stay and let me go .

362
00:36:32,003 --> 00:36:33,493
Helen

363
00:36:34,305 --> 00:36:36,637
you look as though you lost your best friend .

364
00:36:36,808 --> 00:36:38,207
You got nothing to worry about .

365
00:36:38,376 --> 00:36:40,776
If anybody tried any of their funny business on you

366
00:36:40,945 --> 00:36:42,970
I 'd soon sock them in the jaw .

367
00:36:43,314 --> 00:36:45,043
Look at it this way , Helen .

368
00:36:45,216 --> 00:36:47,411
Murder 's like a million-dollar lottery .

369
00:36:47,585 --> 00:36:51,021
Sure , it is . Listen . You pick up the newspaper .

370
00:36:51,222 --> 00:36:53,986
You see someone 's picture who 's won a million dollars .

371
00:36:54,192 --> 00:36:55,682
You pick up another paper .

372
00:36:55,860 --> 00:36:58,055
There 's a picture of someone who 's been murdered .

373
00:36:58,229 --> 00:37:00,720
But it 's never me and it 's never you .

374
00:37:00,899 --> 00:37:02,628
It 's always somebody else , isn 't it ?

375
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:04,597
There 's safety in numbers , Helen .

376
00:37:04,769 --> 00:37:08,535
There 's Oates and me and the professor and Stephen .

377
00:37:08,706 --> 00:37:11,732
- We 'll look after you . - And there 's Carleton too .

378
00:37:12,911 --> 00:37:14,469
Shouldn 't count too much on him .

379
00:37:21,920 --> 00:37:24,980
And there 's Nurse Barker . She 'd be as good as any man .

380
00:37:25,290 --> 00:37:28,088
In fact , sometimes I think she is a man .

381
00:37:29,661 --> 00:37:31,492
In case you 're interested

382
00:37:34,599 --> 00:37:37,363
there 's someone at the front door .

383
00:37:50,081 --> 00:37:52,379
- What do you want ? - I was called to see Mrs. Warren .

384
00:37:52,684 --> 00:37:54,948
It 's Dr. Parry . Was he called ?

385
00:37:56,187 --> 00:37:57,779
Hello , Helen .

386
00:37:58,556 --> 00:38:01,252
I suppose they called Dr. Harvey first .

387
00:38:01,426 --> 00:38:03,223
You mean Mrs. Warren asked for me ?

388
00:38:03,394 --> 00:38:06,227
Well , I 've got me a patient now .

389
00:38:08,266 --> 00:38:12,669
I 'm glad I was called , Helen . I 've wanted to have a long talk with you

390
00:38:13,972 --> 00:38:16,497
and I 'm going to before I leave .

391
00:38:20,211 --> 00:38:23,476
- How are you , Dr. Parry ? - I 'm fine . How are you , Mrs. Warren ?

392
00:38:24,449 --> 00:38:26,815
Did you know my husband ?

393
00:38:27,051 --> 00:38:28,916
No , I didn 't , Mrs. Warren .

394
00:38:29,087 --> 00:38:33,251
Of course not . He died years before you came here .

395
00:38:33,791 --> 00:38:35,986
You 're a little like him .

396
00:38:36,628 --> 00:38:39,927
Firm step , strong hand

397
00:38:40,498 --> 00:38:41,931
good eyes .

398
00:38:42,600 --> 00:38:45,125
Thank you . I know you were very fond of him .

399
00:38:46,237 --> 00:38:49,798
He told me I wasn 't as beautiful as his first wife

400
00:38:49,974 --> 00:38:52,272
but I was a much better shot .

401
00:38:55,113 --> 00:38:58,742
The only kind of beauty he had any respect for was strength .

402
00:38:59,584 --> 00:39:01,677
And he had two sons

403
00:39:01,853 --> 00:39:03,787
both weaklings .

404
00:39:03,955 --> 00:39:07,254
They hated guns and hunting .

405
00:39:07,425 --> 00:39:10,087
He used to run away from them , Dr. Parry .

406
00:39:10,261 --> 00:39:11,660
Well

407
00:39:11,829 --> 00:39:14,923
he got his release from a bottle .

408
00:39:15,099 --> 00:39:19,536
And he died as he lived , happily , extravagantly .

409
00:39:19,704 --> 00:39:21,365
I 'm sorry .

410
00:39:21,539 --> 00:39:23,632
Oh , no . You mustn 't be .

411
00:39:23,808 --> 00:39:26,174
You mustn 't be sorry for him .

412
00:39:26,811 --> 00:39:29,041
You should try to get some rest , Mrs. Warren .

413
00:39:29,213 --> 00:39:33,673
Yes , I know . I talk too much . I talk too much .

414
00:39:37,422 --> 00:39:39,947
- Get Helen out of this house . - Why ?

415
00:39:40,491 --> 00:39:42,823
Because I know you love her .

416
00:39:43,494 --> 00:39:44,825
Take her away .

417
00:39:44,996 --> 00:39:47,123
Promise me you 'll take her away from here .

418
00:39:47,432 --> 00:39:49,195
Very well , I promise .

419
00:39:49,467 --> 00:39:51,901
Take her away tonight .

420
00:39:52,303 --> 00:39:55,466
If it 's money you need , I 'll get it for you .

421
00:40:03,815 --> 00:40:05,908
Get me the ether , Helen .

422
00:40:12,990 --> 00:40:14,514
Did you get it ?

423
00:40:15,059 --> 00:40:16,959
I 'll go ask Nurse Barker .

424
00:40:20,898 --> 00:40:22,661
Come in , please , nurse .

425
00:40:25,536 --> 00:40:27,595
Will you get me the ether ? Helen can 't find it .

426
00:40:27,772 --> 00:40:31,469
It was used about an hour ago . Where did you put it ?

427
00:40:31,642 --> 00:40:33,439
Let 's have another look .

428
00:40:40,585 --> 00:40:44,646
It 's gone , and you 're the only people who have been in this room today .

429
00:40:45,890 --> 00:40:48,415
- Unless Mrs. Warren- - - You took the ether , Barker .

430
00:40:48,593 --> 00:40:51,118
Why , I did no such thing . You always make me sit outside .

431
00:40:51,295 --> 00:40:54,196
Never mind . Maybe Professor Warren will know about it .

432
00:40:54,365 --> 00:40:56,162
I 'll go and see him .

433
00:41:01,105 --> 00:41:03,266
Here , where 's my brandy ?

434
00:41:03,441 --> 00:41:05,909
I finished it for your own good .

435
00:41:06,677 --> 00:41:09,805
Well , I wish you 'd stop doing things for my own good .

436
00:41:10,114 --> 00:41:13,345
With everything that 's happening , it 's better that you keep your wits .

437
00:41:13,518 --> 00:41:16,009
I 'm never more witty than when I 've had a little nip .

438
00:41:16,187 --> 00:41:20,055
I see better , I hear better , and I feel much better .

439
00:41:20,658 --> 00:41:23,786
Oates , would you mind coming out a moment ? Bring your hat and coat .

440
00:41:23,961 --> 00:41:25,622
There it is .

441
00:41:25,863 --> 00:41:28,263
Emma , let 's be serious for a minute .

442
00:41:28,432 --> 00:41:30,297
I want you to stay awake until I get back .

443
00:41:30,468 --> 00:41:32,436
Keep an eye on Helen . I won 't be long .

444
00:41:32,603 --> 00:41:36,630
I could keep a much better eye on Helen if I 'd had a little nip .

445
00:41:39,110 --> 00:41:40,737
I can 't understand .

446
00:41:40,945 --> 00:41:43,072
Ether was used less than two hours ago .

447
00:41:43,247 --> 00:41:45,238
Stephen used it . He said Helen gave it to him .

448
00:41:45,416 --> 00:41:47,441
Unfortunately , I have no other supply .

449
00:41:47,618 --> 00:41:51,452
Oates , I 'm afraid you 'll have to go into the village for some ether .

450
00:41:51,622 --> 00:41:53,715
It 's stormy out . Does it have to be done ?

451
00:41:53,891 --> 00:41:55,916
If it didn 't have to be done , I wouldn 't ask .

452
00:41:56,093 --> 00:41:57,890
All right , all right , I 'll go .

453
00:41:58,062 --> 00:42:00,462
He won 't find any in the village . I tried to get some .

454
00:42:00,631 --> 00:42:02,895
I have to go to Morristown . It 'll take hours .

455
00:42:03,067 --> 00:42:05,262
I 'm sorry , it 's an emergency . We have to have it .

456
00:42:05,536 --> 00:42:07,094
You 're sorry , but I have to go .

457
00:42:07,271 --> 00:42:09,262
You should have some other stimulant at hand .

458
00:42:09,440 --> 00:42:12,238
- Brandy ? I 'll get a bottle . - That will do .

459
00:42:13,010 --> 00:42:16,173
- Will you ask Helen to come for it ? - Yeah .

460
00:42:19,884 --> 00:42:21,545
Mrs. Oates .

461
00:42:22,086 --> 00:42:23,553
Yes , sir ?

462
00:42:23,721 --> 00:42:26,019
Come along with me while I get a bottle of brandy .

463
00:42:26,190 --> 00:42:27,680
Yes , sir .

464
00:43:13,638 --> 00:43:16,835
Oh , dear , now I 've done it .

465
00:43:17,174 --> 00:43:19,142
- Did you bring a match ? - No , sir .

466
00:43:19,310 --> 00:43:22,006
Oh , well , never mind . Perhaps I have one .

467
00:43:22,613 --> 00:43:24,240
Here we are .

468
00:43:26,217 --> 00:43:29,050
I think it rolled over there , sir .

469
00:43:46,170 --> 00:43:48,866
I 'll take it this time , Mrs. Oates .

470
00:43:55,980 --> 00:43:57,845
Your key , sir .

471
00:44:04,455 --> 00:44:06,047
Oh , my .

472
00:44:06,223 --> 00:44:08,157
Did I put one over on him .

473
00:44:08,326 --> 00:44:12,353
Easy as taking candy from a baby . Take a tip from me , Helen .

474
00:44:12,530 --> 00:44:15,158
If you carry the candle to the cellar for the professor

475
00:44:15,333 --> 00:44:18,131
and you fancy a bottle of his fine old brandy

476
00:44:18,302 --> 00:44:22,636
just throw the candle to one side . Accidentally on purpose , of course .

477
00:44:23,040 --> 00:44:25,668
Anything can happen in the dark .

478
00:44:26,177 --> 00:44:27,735
Presto .

479
00:44:32,116 --> 00:44:34,584
Now , I 'll just wipe this off

480
00:44:35,786 --> 00:44:38,186
and you can take it to Dr. Parry .

481
00:44:43,461 --> 00:44:44,985
Helen .

482
00:44:45,496 --> 00:44:47,327
Come into the den . I want to talk to you .

483
00:44:47,498 --> 00:44:49,398
Mrs. Warren 's asleep .

484
00:44:49,967 --> 00:44:52,333
Professor Warren 's with her now .

485
00:44:55,439 --> 00:44:58,806
I 've been thinking things over . And Mrs. Warren 's right .

486
00:44:58,976 --> 00:45:02,070
You should come with me tonight . You can stay at my mother 's place

487
00:45:02,246 --> 00:45:04,874
until we can make arrangements to go to Boston .

488
00:45:05,549 --> 00:45:07,642
My mother will like you .

489
00:45:09,020 --> 00:45:12,319
I don 't wanna frighten you , but you heard Mrs. Warren a while ago .

490
00:45:12,490 --> 00:45:16,358
Her mind 's growing steadily worse , and I 'm afraid she may become violent .

491
00:45:16,527 --> 00:45:20,327
She seems obsessed by the idea that you get out of this house .

492
00:45:20,664 --> 00:45:23,428
And there may be something back of it .

493
00:45:24,969 --> 00:45:27,096
You 'll go with me tonight .

494
00:45:27,271 --> 00:45:30,468
There are doctors in Boston who 'll know all about your case .

495
00:45:30,641 --> 00:45:32,871
I want to take you there .

496
00:45:33,044 --> 00:45:34,568
Helen .

497
00:45:37,314 --> 00:45:39,976
When I left you this afternoon , I dropped in at the Fabers ' .

498
00:45:40,151 --> 00:45:43,314
They have a guest visiting them from your hometown .

499
00:45:43,821 --> 00:45:45,448
A Mrs. Lindstrom .

500
00:45:45,623 --> 00:45:47,250
You know her ?

501
00:45:52,530 --> 00:45:54,088
Well

502
00:45:55,132 --> 00:45:57,794
she told me a story about a girl .

503
00:45:58,636 --> 00:46:01,833
A girl who was on her way home from school one day .

504
00:46:02,139 --> 00:46:04,699
She had good news for her parents .

505
00:46:06,077 --> 00:46:08,511
When she wasn 't far from her home

506
00:46:08,679 --> 00:46:10,977
she heard a fire engine rushing down the street .

507
00:46:11,348 --> 00:46:14,044
She started to run , and when she turned the corner

508
00:46:14,218 --> 00:46:17,187
she saw that it was her home that was in flames .

509
00:46:17,588 --> 00:46:19,522
There was a crowd outside .

510
00:46:19,690 --> 00:46:22,921
She wanted to scream herself , but somehow she couldn 't .

511
00:46:23,094 --> 00:46:24,686
She tried to rush into the house

512
00:46:24,862 --> 00:46:26,887
but was held back because it was hopeless .

513
00:46:27,064 --> 00:46:30,625
So without being able to do one thing to help

514
00:46:30,801 --> 00:46:34,032
she saw her mother and father burn to death .

515
00:46:40,277 --> 00:46:43,041
I 'm sorry , Helen , but I had to do it .

516
00:46:43,948 --> 00:46:45,745
It 's only because I wanted to help you .

517
00:46:45,916 --> 00:46:48,180
Go over everything that happened that day .

518
00:46:48,352 --> 00:46:50,343
Have the courage to see it all again .

519
00:46:50,521 --> 00:46:54,389
And by not blocking it out of your mind , you may find your voice again .

520
00:46:57,628 --> 00:47:00,426
I don 't like being an outsider , and you shouldn 't either .

521
00:47:00,598 --> 00:47:04,329
I know what I 'm talking about because I 'm an outsider here myself .

522
00:47:04,502 --> 00:47:06,834
A lot of people don 't want me . They want me to quit .

523
00:47:07,004 --> 00:47:10,371
But I won 't , because there 's at least one person who wants me here

524
00:47:10,541 --> 00:47:12,509
and that 's good enough for me .

525
00:47:12,676 --> 00:47:14,735
And there 's one person who wants you to talk

526
00:47:14,912 --> 00:47:17,642
and that ought to be good enough for you . Look at me .

527
00:47:17,815 --> 00:47:19,043
Look at me .

528
00:47:19,216 --> 00:47:21,480
Remember how wonderful it was when you had a voice ?

529
00:47:21,652 --> 00:47:23,620
When you could say " hello " or " thank you " ?

530
00:47:23,787 --> 00:47:26,153
When you could yell back at someone picking at you ?

531
00:47:26,323 --> 00:47:27,847
I do it all the time .

532
00:47:28,025 --> 00:47:31,552
You look at me as though you don 't believe it , but I know I 'm right .

533
00:47:31,729 --> 00:47:35,358
Try to talk ! Try it ! Try it !

534
00:47:38,402 --> 00:47:40,199
Excuse me .

535
00:47:42,006 --> 00:47:44,634
My mother is asking for you , Helen .

536
00:47:48,179 --> 00:47:51,012
I 'll speak to Professor Warren about your leaving .

537
00:47:52,816 --> 00:47:55,148
What is this about Helen leaving ?

538
00:47:55,319 --> 00:47:57,014
I 'll discuss it with your brother .

539
00:47:57,188 --> 00:47:59,588
Is it something you can 't discuss with me ?

540
00:47:59,757 --> 00:48:02,658
Why is she leaving ? Where is she going ?

541
00:48:02,826 --> 00:48:06,023
Well , I 've been doing a great deal of thinking about Helen .

542
00:48:06,197 --> 00:48:08,688
I know her condition is due to shock .

543
00:48:08,866 --> 00:48:11,630
I 'm sure a new mental therapy can restore her voice .

544
00:48:11,802 --> 00:48:13,235
I 'd like to take her to Boston .

545
00:48:13,404 --> 00:48:15,531
Aren 't you taking a tremendous responsibility ?

546
00:48:15,706 --> 00:48:17,037
Building up her hopes .

547
00:48:17,208 --> 00:48:19,836
Making her think there 's some miracle in store for her .

548
00:48:20,010 --> 00:48:22,205
It 's up to her , not you .

549
00:48:22,913 --> 00:48:25,780
What you 're doing is cruel and foolish .

550
00:48:26,250 --> 00:48:29,913
That girl is adjusted to her affliction . I think you should let it go at that .

551
00:48:30,087 --> 00:48:32,555
Suppose you let me mind my own business .

552
00:48:32,723 --> 00:48:36,215
It so happens I don 't think much of your business , Dr. Parry .

553
00:48:36,393 --> 00:48:38,156
If there is a solution to her problem

554
00:48:38,329 --> 00:48:41,457
it ought to be in the hands of someone other than a hick doctor .

555
00:48:41,632 --> 00:48:44,226
The thing that keeps me from cracking you in the jaw

556
00:48:44,401 --> 00:48:47,461
is the almost certain possibility that it would break your neck .

557
00:48:47,638 --> 00:48:49,572
What 's the trouble , doctor ?

558
00:48:49,940 --> 00:48:53,068
The good country doctor , having lost his wits

559
00:48:53,244 --> 00:48:55,303
was about to resort to his fists .

560
00:48:55,479 --> 00:48:58,880
Professor Warren , I know you 're interested in Helen 's welfare .

561
00:48:59,049 --> 00:49:02,541
I 've told you what I 've learned . I 've decided it 's for her best interest ...

562
00:49:02,720 --> 00:49:04,813
- ... that she leave here tonight . - Tonight ?

563
00:49:04,989 --> 00:49:07,822
She can stay at my mother 's until we can take her to Boston

564
00:49:07,992 --> 00:49:10,460
for the examination first thing in the morning .

565
00:49:10,928 --> 00:49:12,953
Doctor , you know that I agree with you

566
00:49:13,130 --> 00:49:16,258
about the element of hope that you have for Helen

567
00:49:16,567 --> 00:49:19,968
but what 's your reason for suddenly making her leave tonight ?

568
00:49:20,137 --> 00:49:22,469
Well , Mrs. Warren feels

569
00:49:22,973 --> 00:49:25,100
that she 's in danger here .

570
00:49:29,546 --> 00:49:32,982
Surely you don 't take the ramblings of a sick woman seriously .

571
00:49:33,150 --> 00:49:35,516
I take most things seriously .

572
00:49:35,686 --> 00:49:38,120
But , doctor , there are many other considerations .

573
00:49:38,289 --> 00:49:41,087
Helen needs this position . It 's her only means of support .

574
00:49:41,258 --> 00:49:42,623
No family . It won 't be easy- -

575
00:49:42,793 --> 00:49:45,023
I 've thought of all those things , professor .

576
00:49:45,195 --> 00:49:46,662
I ... .

577
00:49:46,830 --> 00:49:48,821
I intend to take care of her .

578
00:49:49,033 --> 00:49:50,364
Oh , I see .

579
00:49:50,534 --> 00:49:53,094
Well , I 'm very glad for you and for her .

580
00:49:53,270 --> 00:49:54,897
You 're a sentimentalist , doctor .

581
00:49:55,072 --> 00:49:57,131
Are your humanitarian instincts restricted

582
00:49:57,308 --> 00:50:00,038
only to people with serious afflictions ?

583
00:50:03,781 --> 00:50:05,510
You 're very insolent .

584
00:50:05,683 --> 00:50:07,412
Dr. Parry .

585
00:50:13,424 --> 00:50:14,948
Excuse me .

586
00:50:20,297 --> 00:50:21,787
Hello ?

587
00:50:22,166 --> 00:50:25,135
Yes , he is . Just a moment .

588
00:50:26,937 --> 00:50:29,462
- It 's for you , doctor . - Thank you .

589
00:50:31,742 --> 00:50:33,232
Hello ?

590
00:50:35,245 --> 00:50:36,735
Helen

591
00:50:37,481 --> 00:50:39,915
the Wilson boy is sick . I have to go over there .

592
00:50:40,084 --> 00:50:43,542
Now , here 's their phone number . You can pack while I 'm gone .

593
00:50:43,721 --> 00:50:48,090
If you need anything before I get back , have Mrs. Oates call me .

594
00:50:48,392 --> 00:50:50,792
I 'll be back as soon as I can .

595
00:50:54,298 --> 00:50:56,459
Be sure and bar the door behind me .

596
00:50:56,633 --> 00:50:59,363
And don 't let anyone in but me .

597
00:53:03,327 --> 00:53:05,625
Wilt thou obey him

598
00:53:05,796 --> 00:53:07,388
serve him

599
00:53:07,564 --> 00:53:12,661
Iove , honor and keep him , in sickness and in health

600
00:53:12,836 --> 00:53:15,134
and forsaking all others

601
00:53:15,305 --> 00:53:17,967
keep thee only unto him

602
00:53:18,141 --> 00:53:21,702
so long as ye both shall live ?

603
00:53:22,279 --> 00:53:25,612
Signify by saying , " I do . "

604
00:53:28,085 --> 00:53:30,110
Say , " I do . "

605
00:53:31,588 --> 00:53:34,148
Say , " I do . "

606
00:53:35,993 --> 00:53:38,223
Say , " I do . "

607
00:53:39,997 --> 00:53:42,192
Say , " I do . "

608
00:53:44,001 --> 00:53:46,162
Say , " I do . "

609
00:53:47,971 --> 00:53:50,098
Say , " I do . "

610
00:53:51,775 --> 00:53:54,335
Say , " I do . "

611
00:53:55,812 --> 00:53:58,508
Say , " I do . "

612
00:53:59,983 --> 00:54:02,645
Say , " I do . "

613
00:54:10,827 --> 00:54:14,058
What 's the matter , Helen ? Don 't you feel well ?

614
00:54:19,102 --> 00:54:21,434
I understand you 're going to leave us .

615
00:54:21,605 --> 00:54:24,301
Well , I don 't know whether Dr. Parry is right or wrong

616
00:54:24,474 --> 00:54:27,534
but I agree that you should have that chance to go to Boston .

617
00:54:27,711 --> 00:54:31,147
And I want you to understand if things don 't work out satisfactorily

618
00:54:31,315 --> 00:54:33,579
that you 're always welcome to come here .

619
00:54:33,750 --> 00:54:35,809
Now , you run along .

620
00:55:10,354 --> 00:55:12,948
I like to see women cry .

621
00:55:15,993 --> 00:55:20,123
Men like to see women cry . It makes them feel superior .

622
00:55:21,598 --> 00:55:23,429
Oh , Steve

623
00:55:23,667 --> 00:55:25,635
I 'm very unhappy

624
00:55:26,003 --> 00:55:27,265
and upset .

625
00:55:27,437 --> 00:55:29,371
You dramatize everything , Blanche .

626
00:55:29,539 --> 00:55:32,838
We 've been very happy . At least , I have .

627
00:55:33,844 --> 00:55:37,245
- I don 't like your attitude at all . - I 'm sorry .

628
00:55:38,515 --> 00:55:41,973
It 's just , I 'm- - I 'm making trouble between you and your stepbrother .

629
00:55:42,619 --> 00:55:45,247
I don 't like to hide anything I feel .

630
00:55:47,024 --> 00:55:49,049
And you know how I feel about you .

631
00:55:49,459 --> 00:55:51,086
That 's very sweet of you , Blanche .

632
00:55:51,261 --> 00:55:53,456
But are you sure you 're telling me the truth ?

633
00:55:53,630 --> 00:55:55,029
Truth about what ?

634
00:55:55,198 --> 00:55:57,996
Just that I think you 're uncomfortable because of your

635
00:55:58,168 --> 00:56:00,659
past relationship with my brother .

636
00:56:01,505 --> 00:56:03,530
- You are a- - - Don 't say it .

637
00:56:03,874 --> 00:56:06,274
Just answer my question .

638
00:56:12,049 --> 00:56:13,573
Get out .

639
00:56:15,685 --> 00:56:18,210
Don 't be so melodramatic .

640
00:56:19,956 --> 00:56:22,891
I didn 't realize you were so strong .

641
00:56:23,060 --> 00:56:24,584
I 'm leaving here .

642
00:56:24,761 --> 00:56:26,490
I never want to see you again .

643
00:56:26,663 --> 00:56:28,392
I 'll miss you .

644
00:56:28,565 --> 00:56:30,692
A house like this needs charm .

645
00:56:30,867 --> 00:56:33,734
I told you to get out .

646
00:56:33,904 --> 00:56:35,804
You 're going to regret this .

647
00:56:57,327 --> 00:56:59,659
I 'm sorry to intrude , Helen .

648
00:56:59,830 --> 00:57:01,229
I have a favor to ask of you .

649
00:57:01,398 --> 00:57:05,095
You 're leaving tonight , and I want to go into town with you .

650
00:57:07,370 --> 00:57:08,894
I 'm happy for you .

651
00:57:09,072 --> 00:57:11,836
Things will be so different when you 're cured .

652
00:57:12,242 --> 00:57:15,905
I don 't know what will become of me , but I 've got to leave this house .

653
00:57:16,079 --> 00:57:18,513
It hasn 't been good for anyone here .

654
00:57:19,983 --> 00:57:21,644
I 'm only taking a few things with me .

655
00:57:21,818 --> 00:57:24,286
Oates can pick up my other things tomorrow .

656
00:57:24,821 --> 00:57:28,188
My suitcase is in the basement . I 'll only be a few minutes .

657
00:57:47,277 --> 00:57:50,007
This is the second time I 've closed that window tonight .

658
00:57:50,180 --> 00:57:52,614
I definitely know I did .

659
00:57:52,782 --> 00:57:55,512
Now , if only I knew who opened it .

660
00:57:55,685 --> 00:57:59,917
You 're not that clever , and if you were ... .

661
01:00:23,433 --> 01:00:27,961
Oh , it 's you . You scared the life out of me .

662
01:01:17,887 --> 01:01:20,447
I told you not to touch me . Get out .

663
01:01:20,623 --> 01:01:23,456
I 'll get out , Mrs. Warren . Not only out of here ...

664
01:01:23,626 --> 01:01:25,491
- ... but out of this house . - Good riddance .

665
01:01:25,662 --> 01:01:28,825
But before I go , you 're going to hear a few things .

666
01:01:29,099 --> 01:01:31,727
I 'm tired of being a target for an evil old woman .

667
01:01:31,901 --> 01:01:33,368
Nobody 's asking you to stay .

668
01:01:33,536 --> 01:01:35,663
If you got down on your knees , I wouldn 't stay .

669
01:01:35,839 --> 01:01:37,830
- I don 't need this job . - Why don 't you go ?

670
01:01:38,007 --> 01:01:42,444
You need a keeper , not a nurse . I don 't care if you never walk again .

671
01:01:42,612 --> 01:01:45,376
You can stay in that bed for the rest of your life .

672
01:01:45,682 --> 01:01:48,048
I 've taken everything , but I 'll not put up with this .

673
01:01:48,218 --> 01:01:50,311
I 'm leaving this house tonight .

674
01:02:02,198 --> 01:02:04,223
I 'll soon clear them out .

675
01:02:04,401 --> 01:02:07,199
I hate nurses . Always fussing .

676
01:02:07,370 --> 01:02:09,895
Always washing your face .

677
01:02:14,978 --> 01:02:16,570
Helen .

678
01:02:17,680 --> 01:02:22,242
Did you know there was a girl murdered here a long time ago ?

679
01:02:24,621 --> 01:02:26,589
I saw it .

680
01:02:27,290 --> 01:02:30,157
Upstairs , from the window .

681
01:02:30,527 --> 01:02:31,960
It was getting dark .

682
01:02:32,595 --> 01:02:36,087
I thought it was a tree in the garden .

683
01:02:37,100 --> 01:02:39,898
Stood so still

684
01:02:40,370 --> 01:02:42,201
and waited .

685
01:02:42,906 --> 01:02:48,173
Then when the poor , simple-minded creature came near the house

686
01:02:48,745 --> 01:02:50,838
the tree moved

687
01:02:51,014 --> 01:02:53,482
threw her into the well .

688
01:02:54,784 --> 01:02:56,843
I was too late .

689
01:02:57,220 --> 01:02:59,654
I couldn 't find the rope .

690
01:03:03,860 --> 01:03:05,794
You were that girl , Helen .

691
01:03:11,267 --> 01:03:13,030
Come here .

692
01:03:14,971 --> 01:03:16,598
Come here .

693
01:03:19,609 --> 01:03:21,440
You must go away .

694
01:03:21,611 --> 01:03:23,340
Leave this house .

695
01:03:23,513 --> 01:03:25,913
Go with Nurse Barker tonight .

696
01:03:26,082 --> 01:03:29,745
Don 't wait for Dr. Parry . Don 't wait for anyone .

697
01:03:30,653 --> 01:03:34,111
If you won 't , you must do what I tell you .

698
01:03:34,691 --> 01:03:36,659
You must get under the bed .

699
01:03:36,826 --> 01:03:38,418
Do you understand ?

700
01:03:38,595 --> 01:03:41,860
You must hide under the bed .

701
01:03:42,832 --> 01:03:46,290
Why won 't you do what I tell you to ?

702
01:03:46,703 --> 01:03:49,171
Why won 't you listen to me ?

703
01:03:49,339 --> 01:03:52,467
Why won 't anyone listen to me ?

704
01:04:10,493 --> 01:04:12,484
Would you mind letting me have a wagon ?

705
01:04:12,662 --> 01:04:15,256
I 'll leave it in the village for Oates to pick up .

706
01:04:15,431 --> 01:04:18,059
Very well . I 'll go out with you and hitch up the wagon .

707
01:04:18,234 --> 01:04:20,464
You 're very kind , professor .

708
01:04:37,854 --> 01:04:39,549
I 've been walking .

709
01:04:40,023 --> 01:04:42,389
- In this rain ? - Yes .

710
01:04:42,559 --> 01:04:44,254
In this rain .

711
01:04:45,161 --> 01:04:47,994
I wonder if you 'd mind doing something for me , Stephen .

712
01:04:48,998 --> 01:04:50,488
What ?

713
01:04:50,667 --> 01:04:52,464
Nurse Barker is leaving us .

714
01:04:52,635 --> 01:04:55,103
And as long as you 're already rather wet

715
01:04:55,271 --> 01:04:57,933
perhaps you wouldn 't mind hitching up the wagon for her .

716
01:04:58,107 --> 01:05:00,405
Everybody 's leaving the old homestead .

717
01:05:00,577 --> 01:05:02,408
Like a holiday .

718
01:05:03,813 --> 01:05:06,247
- It 'll be a pleasure . - For both of us .

719
01:05:06,649 --> 01:05:09,243
- Goodbye , Professor Warren . - Goodbye .

720
01:05:10,286 --> 01:05:13,983
Oh , Helen , will you tell Blanche I want to see her in the den ?

721
01:07:58,354 --> 01:08:00,288
Have you been here long ?

722
01:08:01,657 --> 01:08:04,922
I was outside with Nurse Barker . I saw the basement door open .

723
01:08:05,094 --> 01:08:07,119
Did you come in that way ?

724
01:08:08,131 --> 01:08:09,621
Helen

725
01:08:09,799 --> 01:08:12,359
you must forget everything you 've seen here .

726
01:08:12,535 --> 01:08:16,369
Let me handle this . Do you understand ?

727
01:08:20,743 --> 01:08:22,608
Take the candle .

728
01:08:39,929 --> 01:08:41,692
Come with me .

729
01:08:49,705 --> 01:08:52,037
You don 't think I did it .

730
01:09:05,321 --> 01:09:06,811
Wait .

731
01:09:06,989 --> 01:09:09,150
I think I have a match . Yes .

732
01:09:10,359 --> 01:09:12,259
Where could it go ?

733
01:09:18,234 --> 01:09:19,997
Hey , there it is .

734
01:09:21,804 --> 01:09:23,362
Helen !

735
01:09:23,539 --> 01:09:25,131
Helen !

736
01:09:25,508 --> 01:09:27,499
Let me out of here !

737
01:09:27,877 --> 01:09:29,469
Helen !

738
01:10:35,311 --> 01:10:37,302
Number , please .

739
01:10:38,614 --> 01:10:40,047
Hello .

740
01:10:40,216 --> 01:10:42,116
Number , please .

741
01:10:42,285 --> 01:10:45,516
Hello . Number , please .

742
01:10:51,027 --> 01:10:52,358
Helen .

743
01:10:52,528 --> 01:10:53,927
Helen .

744
01:10:56,232 --> 01:10:59,497
What on earth are you doing ? What 's the matter ?

745
01:11:09,111 --> 01:11:10,442
" Blanche murdered " ?

746
01:11:19,789 --> 01:11:21,347
" Stephen . "

747
01:11:21,724 --> 01:11:23,248
Where ?

748
01:11:27,196 --> 01:11:29,630
I 'll take you up to my stepmother 's room .

749
01:11:29,799 --> 01:11:31,858
You stay there with her .

750
01:11:32,034 --> 01:11:34,298
I 'll call the constable .

751
01:11:36,172 --> 01:11:38,766
Let me take care of things now .

752
01:11:39,208 --> 01:11:41,199
You 've been through enough .

753
01:11:41,377 --> 01:11:43,868
You tried to telephone , didn 't you ?

754
01:11:44,180 --> 01:11:46,614
Well , I 'm glad you couldn 't .

755
01:11:50,653 --> 01:11:53,679
You looked in this mirror once before today .

756
01:11:54,256 --> 01:11:56,190
I watched you .

757
01:11:57,360 --> 01:11:59,590
You had no mouth then .

758
01:11:59,862 --> 01:12:02,126
Just as you have none now .

759
01:12:03,032 --> 01:12:04,966
Look at yourself .

760
01:12:05,901 --> 01:12:07,232
Look .

761
01:12:20,983 --> 01:12:24,510
And there 's no room in the whole world

762
01:12:24,687 --> 01:12:26,882
for imperfection .

763
01:12:27,990 --> 01:12:30,083
The only person who could have prevented you

764
01:12:30,259 --> 01:12:32,853
from achieving the quiet that I can give you

765
01:12:33,029 --> 01:12:34,792
was Stephen .

766
01:12:35,197 --> 01:12:36,824
And you locked him up

767
01:12:37,166 --> 01:12:38,997
downstairs .

768
01:12:46,275 --> 01:12:48,800
We 're quiet now , Helen .

769
01:12:49,545 --> 01:12:51,740
I 'm glad I waited .

770
01:12:52,181 --> 01:12:54,547
Everyone 's out of the way .

771
01:12:55,217 --> 01:12:57,515
Mrs. Oates is drunk

772
01:12:58,187 --> 01:13:01,884
because I purposely let her steal a bottle of brandy .

773
01:13:02,124 --> 01:13:03,682
And Oates

774
01:13:03,859 --> 01:13:05,884
he 's gone to look for ether

775
01:13:06,062 --> 01:13:09,259
because I made sure there was no ether .

776
01:13:09,665 --> 01:13:11,724
And Blanche

777
01:13:11,901 --> 01:13:13,766
whom I loved

778
01:13:14,270 --> 01:13:15,532
didn 't love me

779
01:13:16,105 --> 01:13:17,800
so she had to die .

780
01:13:17,973 --> 01:13:20,373
She 's dead and at peace .

781
01:13:20,709 --> 01:13:22,506
And Stephen

782
01:13:22,745 --> 01:13:25,145
you took care of him for me .

783
01:13:26,082 --> 01:13:28,175
Stephen is weak

784
01:13:28,350 --> 01:13:30,375
as I once was .

785
01:13:30,719 --> 01:13:34,246
What a pity my father didn 't live to see me become strong .

786
01:13:34,523 --> 01:13:36,616
To see me dispose of the weak and imperfects

787
01:13:36,792 --> 01:13:38,316
of the world , whom he detested .

788
01:13:40,496 --> 01:13:43,693
He would have admired me for what I 'm going to do .

789
01:14:48,831 --> 01:14:52,028
- Who is it ? - It 's me , the constable .

790
01:14:55,237 --> 01:14:56,704
I met Dr. Parry in town .

791
01:14:56,872 --> 01:14:59,170
He said he won 't be able to pick Helen up tonight .

792
01:14:59,341 --> 01:15:01,468
The boy is very sick , and he has to stay there .

793
01:15:01,644 --> 01:15:04,112
Oh , I 'm sorry to hear that . I 'll tell her , constable .

794
01:15:04,280 --> 01:15:07,215
Well , I 'll be on my way then . Good night .

795
01:16:58,460 --> 01:17:00,257
Helen !

796
01:18:32,154 --> 01:18:33,951
Helen !

797
01:18:34,423 --> 01:18:36,220
Helen !

798
01:19:00,482 --> 01:19:02,006
Helen !

799
01:19:04,486 --> 01:19:06,249
Helen !

800
01:19:36,351 --> 01:19:37,613
Murderer .

801
01:19:38,754 --> 01:19:40,483
Helen !

802
01:19:49,198 --> 01:19:51,029
You killed them .

803
01:19:51,600 --> 01:19:53,090
You killed them all .

804
01:19:53,936 --> 01:19:55,836
The servant girl in the well .

805
01:19:57,005 --> 01:19:59,439
The others in the town .

806
01:19:59,708 --> 01:20:03,144
Today , the cripple in the hotel .

807
01:20:03,779 --> 01:20:06,009
You killed them all .

808
01:20:06,648 --> 01:20:10,243
Tonight , it would have been Helen .

809
01:20:11,386 --> 01:20:13,445
I heard you .

810
01:20:14,389 --> 01:20:16,152
Stephen .

811
01:20:16,325 --> 01:20:18,452
Get me Stephen .

812
01:20:53,061 --> 01:20:54,824
Now it 's been done .

813
01:20:58,333 --> 01:21:01,166
Ten years too late .

814
01:21:05,374 --> 01:21:07,069
No .

815
01:21:16,852 --> 01:21:19,082
Forgive me , Stephen .

816
01:21:19,655 --> 01:21:21,919
I thought it was you .

817
01:21:22,090 --> 01:21:25,651
He always waited till you came home

818
01:21:25,994 --> 01:21:28,792
so I thought it was you .

819
01:21:32,200 --> 01:21:35,761
A doctor . Get Dr. Parry . Hurry !

820
01:22:06,902 --> 01:22:08,460
One

821
01:22:11,006 --> 01:22:12,564
eight

822
01:22:15,177 --> 01:22:16,838
nine .

823
01:22:22,417 --> 01:22:24,510
Dr. Parry .

824
01:22:24,886 --> 01:22:26,410
Come .

825
01:22:28,724 --> 01:22:31,955
It 's I , Helen .

